The '''Time Grappler''' was a [[human]] who resided on [[Ferrix]]. It was his duty to ring in the beginning and end of each [[Standard day|day]] by striking<ref name="That Would Be Me" /> a [[beskar]] anvil<ref name="Audio" /> atop a [[Ferrix bell tower|bell tower]] on [[Rix Road]]. The Time Grappler handled this task with reverence, adopting rhythmic poses before each [[Hammer (tool)|hammer]] strike. He wore a set of earmuffs to protect his hearing from the anvil's clangs.<ref name="That Would Be Me" />

In [[5 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{AndorDate|102}}</ref> like any other day, the Time Grappler woke the people of Ferrix on the morning that a number of [[Pre-Mor Authority Security Forces|Pre-Mor Enforcement]] [[Tac-Corpo|Corpos]] came to the [[planet]] in search of [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]]. The off-worlders found themselves unwelcome; their arrival sent the locals off on ringing a series of metal fixtures throughout the population center, much like the Time Grappler would strike his own anvil. These tensions culminated in an [[Ambush on Ferrix|explosive encounter]] on Rix Road that saw Andor escape the planet.<ref name="That Would Be Me" />

Against the wishes of the Imperial authorities that had established themselves on the planet, the Time Grappler signaled the beginning of [[Maarva Carassi Andor|Maarva Andor's]] [[Maarva's funeral procession|funeral]] two hours before schedule at midday, forcing a hurried response by the Imperial army troopers at the scene. When a posthumous speech by the late Andor led the crowd to spontaneously erupt into a [[Ferrix Riot|riot]] and a bomb led to the riot becoming a bloodbath, the clanging continued. A single [[stormtrooper]] was ordered to climb the tower, apprehend the Time Grappler and stop the clanging by Imperial [[Lieutenant]] [[Merzin Keysax]], but was kicked off and fell to his death.<ref name="Rix Road">{{Andor|Rix Road (episode)}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Time Grappler appeared in "[[That Would Be Me]]," the second episode of the [[2022]] [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', where he was portrayed by [[Neil Bell]].<ref name="That Would Be Me" /> He was first seen in the show's teaser trailer, which revealed the character's title in the closed captions.<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|j5UX1Adanis|Andor &#124; Teaser Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/andor-teaser-trailer}}</ref>

